<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan MFIG group buys 54,000T U.S. corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan MFIG group buys 54,000T U.S. corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Members Feed Industry Group bought a 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. No.2 corn from Japanese's trading house Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd at a tender on Thursday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The feed group's main buyers are Taiwan's Formosa Oilseed, Fomau Cereal, Morn Sun Feed Mill and Shin Tai Industry.</p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>Tonnage Date/Location</p>
<p>	   U.S. Gulf    Pacific N.W.	     Prices</p>
<p>54,000  August 6-20  August 21-September 5  $122.74</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (886-2-5080815)</p>
